    "date": "2026-11-18",
    "comparison": "A registered count-growth DEC-35; B appends one full SCL4096 query on the absolute-residual top pattern only at a K-1 pre-completion fit; C replaces the selector by the verified all-magnitude/common-signed-prefix one-slot likelihood. Terminal discovery keeps the complete bank, then refits and completes. Full IID source, original balanced B100, 87 payload, CRC16, Nc512, P8192, n30000, K100, Eb/N0 .5dB, known K and noise, with replacement. No assumed correct cancellation, supplied patterns, repeated-word filters or bank exclusions.",
    "panel": "7501..7628 frame0 inclusive; 128 previously unused geometry/source seeds, RNG [671129,seed,0]. No identifying existing frame artifacts in repository at declaration. All 128 enter the comparison, including ineligible states. No additional seeds or changes to repair a failed gate.",
    "factorization": "Each of B,C is implemented as the complete ordinary count-growth receiver followed by an optional terminal operation after its original completion; recover the pre-completion fit from the immutable baseline metadata. The original terminal action is never fed back into the SCL residual. The cold receiver is exactly common before either selector. Execute this single unchanged prefix once per physical frame, independently run both terminal operations in alternating order on the same pristine fitted state, charge its full external wall and geometry once to EVERY standalone policy, including the original completion. Refit/ordinary completion after an extension is also charged. Report common-path standalone times explicitly, not as three independent cold timings. Separately rerun each complete B/C ordinary entry point on the first and last frame and the first eligible frame in each panel half (deduplicated), comparing baseline, extension and final action with staged evaluation. Keep these diagnostic times separate.",
    "gates": "No changes from development: each selector requires >=4 net saved copies over A, >=3 improved frames, net gain >=2 after removal of best frame, maximum single-frame miss regression <=1, complete/converged legal actions, verified source/metric/normal-entry consistency. Unique folded attribution also requires >=2 net saved over B, at least two better frames and >=1 newly retained true ID absent from the magnitude arm on a different selected pattern. B may advance alone. Report false outputs, bank-floor and cost explicitly. Development elapsed times give no fresh runtime gate. A passing all-frame tradeoff and independent audit license the corresponding DEC-35 option.",
    "audit": "Freeze source/evidence and passing finite + development checks before generating fresh frames. Compare all baseline physical input hashes and candidate/fit/output chronology with available ordinary-entry replays. Independent outcome audit regenerates physical data on every terminal-eligible frame; binds all 128 raw frame snapshots and actions and rechecks gates/false/cost sums; for each eligible reconstruct all-pattern rank selections and winning SCL lists against ordinary code on at least first and last eligible of each panel half; independently recompute final counts/fit objective for all eligible. State coverage for the shared upstream prefix explicitly. No external state-of-the-art performance or full adaptive posterior claim follows."
  },
